And then we add Alberta's trucking rules beside 511

This part is critical.

511 alone is not enough to create a legal heavy-truck routing system.

Alberta separately publishes restrictions concerning things such as:

road bans

seasonal weights

restricted bridges

tridem restrictions

vertical bridge clearances

lane restrictions

overweight/oversize permits.


Alberta specifically notes that local road bans may be controlled by the municipality or county rather than the province. 

So I would build another layer:

LEASEOS ROAD AUTHORITY DATABASE

Containing:

Province
Municipality
County / MD
Forestry / resource road
Private road
Lease road
First Nation road

That is especially important for oilfield work.


